WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.002
-There is damming new evidence

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.638
of Donald Trump's plan
to overthrow our democracy.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.039
Meanwhile, Republican governors

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:10.109
are standing in the way
of basic mitigation efforts

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.545
against the surging
COVID-19 Delta variant.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.847
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:18.451
♪♪

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.819
We promise to stop talking
about Donald Trump

00:00:20.819 --> 00:00:22.822
the day he stops talking.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.590
But, even now that he's
out of office,

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.359
Trump and his movement
always find new ways to shock.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:30.296
For example, the self-labeled
America First movement

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.598
has taken up a new cause --

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:34.834
rooting against American
national sports teams.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.536
-The U.S. Women's Soccer Team

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.704
is a very good example
of what's going on.

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:42.241
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.310
-[ Shouts indistinctly ]

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:48.347
-Earlier this week,
they unexpectedly lost

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:51.317
to Sweden 3-0.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:55.321
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:55.321 --> 00:01:00.793
And Americans were happy
about it.

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:03.362
You proved that point
before I even said it.

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:04.363
Look at the soccer team,

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:05.598
the women's soccer team.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.933
All of a sudden, they're not --
like they were --

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:09.568
they were supposed
to win the gold medal.

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:12.504
But you know the word woke
means "loser."

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:13.539
If you're woke,

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:14.674
[ Laughter ]
you're going to lose.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.542
-First of all, love this conceit

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.477
that Trump follows
women's soccer.

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:19.812
[ As Trump ]
I can't believe nobody

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.947
got a foot on that cross
when you're down 2-nil.

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:24.617
That's what happens
when you're woke.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:28.154
[ Laughter ]
You don't react to the crosses.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.590
You're a former U.S. president
rooting

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.592
against a U.S.
national sports team?

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.762
You, the guy who consistently
went to third base

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:38.063
with the American flag?
A former President

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:40.132
[ Laughter ]
rooting against a U.S.
national team

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:43.102
is like Mr. Met showing up
to a game in a Yankees Jersey.

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.304
Although, after this weekend,
I wouldn't blame him.

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:46.505
When he saw Sunday's box score,

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.942
the Mets-loving
Cigarette Smoking Cockroach

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.843
started lamenting
his immortality.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.445
[ Raspy smoker's voice ]
I can't believe I'm going
to live forever

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.947
and never see this team
win it all.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.149
You thought, just because we
were on a two-week hiatus,

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.385
we wouldn't immediately
come busting out of the gate

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.053
with some callbacks
from recurring characters?

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:03.690
Well, then, I guess you
have a worse memory

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.091
than the crew of the Enterprise,

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.525
when they got stuck
in that time loop.

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.861
[ Laughter ]
"TNG," the new "M-A-S-H"?

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.229
Make it so.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.598
The U.S. women's soccer team
has been wildly successful

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:14.400
and, on top of that,
no one on the team

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.670
ever singlehandedly drove
a sports league into the ground

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.271
like Trump did with the USFL.

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:20.306
If you don't remember
that story,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.007
Trump bought a USFL,

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.742
or United States
Football League, team,

00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:25.778
moved the league
from the spring to the fall,

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:26.913
to compete with the NFL,

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.280
or the National Football League,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.748
which you probably remember
because they're,

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:33.786
you know, still here,
sued the NFL for $1.69 billion

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.589
and was awarded exactly $1
by the jury.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.123
And I have to say,
hats off to that jury

00:02:38.123 --> 00:02:41.694
because it is very funny
to reward someone $1

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.397
after they sue
for almost $1.7 billion.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.932
That's like giving
your employees a holiday bonus

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:49.302
of a Starbucks gift card
with 50 cents on it.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.371
Hi, what can I get
for 50 cents?

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:54.173
"You can, uh,
get out of the [bleep] way."

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.108
[ Laughter ]
There's also a chance

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:58.611
the jury knew Trump
would keep suing,

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:00.680
unless they gave him something
to save face.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.048
"You get nothing."

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.482
[ As Trump ] This isn't
the last you'll hear from me.

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:04.483
"You get a dollar."

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:05.751
[ As Trump ]
And, once again,

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:07.787
Donald Trump is
in the winner's circle.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.321
[ Laughter ]
Oh, it ripped!

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:11.824
[ Laughter ]
Also, I'm not sure

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.327
the massively successful
U.S. Women's Soccer Team,

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:17.296
which has won four World Cups,
including in 2019,

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:18.865
should have to listen
to lessons on winning

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.733
from a guy
who doesn't even know how

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.802
to hold a soccer ball,
much less kick one.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.571
Remember when Putin gave him one
as a gift in Helsinki

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:28.641
and he held it like he thought
it was a precious dinosaur egg?

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.744
That's the way your 40-year-old
single friend holds a baby.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.713
"Oh, no, no, no, no. Okay,
take it back. Take it back."

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.214
[ Laughter ]
He's holding that thing

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.649
like he thinks it's going
to bite him.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.984
It reminds me of Bloomberg

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.453
holding Staten Island Chuck
on Groundhog Day.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.321
Interesting fact -- that day,
Bloomberg saw his shadow

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:43.822
and decided to run
for president.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:46.292
Same thing happened
to de Blasio, so.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.460
Maybe Trump is just mad

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.195
because the U.S. women's
national team is both

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.697
more successful
and more popular than he is.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.866
They've smashed viewership
and merchandise records.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.002
Meanwhile,
a new poll from Quinnipiac

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.103
last week found that...

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:03.910
...while just...

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.048
A full 60% don't want him
to run again.

00:04:10.048 --> 00:04:12.151
That means even some
of the people who voted for him

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:15.254
are like, "I don't know if I can
put myself through that again."

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.623
It's like how no one
does "Hot Ones" twice.

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:18.791
I mean, I did it and loved it,

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.259
but, the next time
I got interviewed,

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:23.762
it was back to the non-spicy
stylings of Terry Gross,

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:25.531
where I was asked
thoughtful questions

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.166
while not worrying
if I was going

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.734
to [bleep] my pants mid-answer.

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.737
[ Laughter ]
"I'm sorry,

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:33.139
is that your stomach
making those noises?"

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.374
Um, it is, Terry,

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:37.109
and I think
I should probably go.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:38.845
[ Laughter ]
Still, that 32%

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:40.179
is always just going
to be shocking to me.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.214
Four years of chaos
and corruption

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:44.650
that ended with all of us
being trapped in our houses,

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.820
using cardboard for toilet paper
to avoid a deadly plague

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.221
the president said
could be cured

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:52.024
by snacking on Tide Pods
like cheese balls,

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:56.028
and, still, 32% of the country
says, "Yes, more of that."

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:58.030
It's insane.
It's the same thing that I get

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.432
when I'm driving around
in the suburbs

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.834
and I see
a Honey Baked Ham store.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.703
People like ham that much?

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.371
I mean, there are
enough people who like

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:09.776
slimy, uncut, wet lunch meat
to keep a chain,

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:12.445
a national chain,
of stores in business?

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.246
I mean, sometimes I park
across from the store,

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:16.715
just to see what kind of maniac
is going in

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:19.585
on a Friday afternoon
and just buying a whole-ass ham.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.721
[ Laughter ]
And then, they send security out

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:24.556
and they tell me I'm the maniac
for sitting there watching.

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:26.559
Like, "Hey, it's America!

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.494
I can watch the ham store."

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.162
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:32.164
But this is why they need
to rig elections to win --

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:33.499
because they're so unpopular.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.768
In a way,
I guess it's not surprising

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.937
that the people rooting
against American sports

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.105
also tried to dismantle
American democracy.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:42.207
And, now, we have
more proof than ever

00:05:42.207 --> 00:05:44.243
that Trump's attempt
to subvert last year's election

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.879
wasn't just a mood swing
or temper tantrum.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.682
There was a detailed plan,
with key allies

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.150
in the White House
and Justice Department,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.185
including one particular
hatchet man

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:54.386
who came incredibly close

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:55.988
to detonating
American democracy.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.290
-Just days before the deadly

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.458
January 6th assault
on the Capitol,

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:00.860
one of the ex-president's

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.729
top Department of Justice
officials at the time

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.931
was circulating a draft letter

00:06:05.931 --> 00:06:08.033
that would've helped
Georgia Republicans

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:10.803
overturn Biden's victory
in that state.

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.805
Jeffrey Clark,
who was the acting head

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:15.541
of the Justice Department's
Civil Division at the time,

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:18.644
wrote emails that essentially
would've laid out a roadmap

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:21.314
and given permission
for Georgia Republicans

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:23.282
to subvert the election results.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.617
-It says in part...

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.292
-How is it that there's always
a smoking gun with these guys?

00:07:07.292 --> 00:07:09.394
There's always an email
or a phone call

00:07:09.394 --> 00:07:12.498
or an accidental televised
confession from Rudy Giuliani

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:13.699
proving our worst fears?

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.500
Like you can be forgiven
for thinking

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:18.070
a petulant Trump just got mad
and decided on a whim

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.539
to call the election rigged
and then, he sent Rudy

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:22.842
to hold a press conference
at a landscaping company,

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:25.477
where I'm guessing he also got
his hair cut by a hedge trimmer,

00:07:25.477 --> 00:07:27.279
and then, it all just kind of
snowballed from there.

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:30.282
But no, Rudy, he was just
a helpful smokescreen

00:07:30.282 --> 00:07:32.418
that let us all think,
"That's too crazy to work."

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:35.688
But they had a much more
sophisticated plan than that.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:38.758
This guy, Jeffrey Clark, a key
Justice Department official,

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:41.127
was going to send a letter
to Georgia's governor

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:43.229
and state legislature,
essentially telling them

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:45.531
to overturn their state's
election results,

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.633
on the basis
of nonexistent voter fraud.

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.135
And it wasn't just Georgia.

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:51.269
He was going to send it
to all the swing states

00:07:51.269 --> 00:07:52.671
Trump wanted to overturn.

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:56.008
-It turns out that this guy,
Jeff Clark,

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:58.443
was writing or drafting
these types of letters

00:07:58.443 --> 00:08:03.316
to all the six states that
ended up going for Joe Biden.

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:06.519
And I think that, you know,

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:08.588
what we see is the beginning

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:10.822
of the effort
to overturn the election.

00:08:10.822 --> 00:08:12.791
-There's always an obscure
functionary willing

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:14.093
to do the villains dirty work.

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:16.929
Jeffrey Clark's like the guy
who opens the monkey cage

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:18.630
in the first five minutes
of a zombie movie.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.566
I mean, can you imagine
what would've happened if,

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:23.402
not Trump, but the
Trump Justice Department,

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:24.971
sent out an official statement

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:26.472
claiming there was fraud
in the election

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:29.174
and telling Republican
legislatures in six states

00:08:29.174 --> 00:08:30.376
to overturn the results?

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.011
Mike Lindell would've exploded

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.345
into a thousand pillow feathers.

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:36.449
Or, I guess, since it's
a MyPillow, he would've exploded

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:38.183
into a thousand
charcoal briquettes.

00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:39.885
[ As Lindell ]
The charcoal gives the pillow

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:41.987
its patented rock-like texture

00:08:41.987 --> 00:08:45.724
and helps you wake up
with that fresh hickory smell.

00:08:45.724 --> 00:08:49.094
Anyway, I'll take two
of your biggest hams!

00:08:49.094 --> 00:08:50.763
[ Laughter ]
You should know

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:53.965
there's a guy peeping in his car
out front, by the way.

00:08:53.965 --> 00:08:55.701
This ham is delicious.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:09:00.339
Usually, I get my lunch meats
from Da Boar's Head!

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:06.979
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:08.280
I'm so happy to be back.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.382
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:12.584
It's easy to write off Trump
and his cronies

00:09:12.584 --> 00:09:14.720
as a bunch of idiot goofballs --
which they were --

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.255
but they also had
a very real plan

00:09:17.255 --> 00:09:19.692
with key allies at the top
levels of the White House,

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:20.826
the Justice Department,

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:22.694
and state legislatures
across the country

00:09:22.694 --> 00:09:25.163
that came extremely close
to nuking American democracy

00:09:25.163 --> 00:09:27.733
and plunging us
into an unprecedented crisis.

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:28.968
The only thing that stopped them

00:09:28.968 --> 00:09:31.303
was senior DOJ leadership
threatening to quit.

00:09:31.303 --> 00:09:34.072
But just imagine if the next
Republican president

00:09:34.072 --> 00:09:36.942
socks the DOJ with loyalists
who follow his orders

00:09:36.942 --> 00:09:39.211
or a Republican-controlled
Congress refuses

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.812
to certify a Democratic victory.

00:09:40.812 --> 00:09:42.148
What then?

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:44.050
We can't just hope the next
coup attempt falls apart

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:47.219
when Rudy Giuliani accidentally
shows up at the wrong location.

00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:49.321
[ As Giuliani ]
Boss, I'm at the Walmart
in Astoria.

00:09:49.321 --> 00:09:51.190
[ As Trump ]
I said the Waldorf Astoria.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.458
[ As Giuliani ]
Oh, Rudy, you done it again!

00:09:53.458 --> 00:09:55.861
[ Laughter ]
We all know

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:57.830
all of this was orchestrated
by Trump

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.231
and his chief of staff,
Mark Meadows,

00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:01.300
because we have the DOJ memos
to prove it.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.903
Trump told the acting
attorney general, Jeffrey Rosen,

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:06.372
at the time, the guy Clark
was trying to replace,

00:10:06.372 --> 00:10:09.140
that he wanted the DOJ
to declare the election rigged,

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:11.376
so he and Republicans
in Congress could overturn it.

00:10:11.376 --> 00:10:14.280
Trump told DOJ leaders,
according to the memos...

00:10:19.752 --> 00:10:21.620
Anytime Trump says,
"Leave the rest to me,"

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.621
you're going to be in trouble.

00:10:22.621 --> 00:10:23.622
I'm sure that's what he said

00:10:23.622 --> 00:10:25.023
to the other USFL owners

00:10:25.023 --> 00:10:26.258
right before he sued the NFL,

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:27.893
only to show up
a few months later asking --

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:30.462
[ As Trump ]
What's a dollar split 18 ways?

00:10:30.462 --> 00:10:32.131
And, yet, even as we learn more

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:34.400
about Trump's attempt
to overthrow the election

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.068
and his sinking popularity
in polls,

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:38.236
he and his supporters are trying
to concoct a fantasy world

00:10:38.236 --> 00:10:40.338
where the chaos, misery,
incompetence,

00:10:40.338 --> 00:10:41.774
and mass suffering
of the Trump era

00:10:41.774 --> 00:10:42.875
was actually popular and good.

00:10:42.875 --> 00:10:46.211
Trump's big, wet,
honey-baked son Don Jr.

00:10:46.211 --> 00:10:48.614
said basically the same thing
on Fox last week.

00:10:48.614 --> 00:10:51.417
-Joe Biden's only legacy,
Sean, at this point,

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:53.018
is going to be showing America

00:10:53.018 --> 00:10:55.921
how good they actually had it
under Donald Trump.

00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:57.890
-I don't know. I feel like
Biden's legacy is going to be,

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.492
as the EMT who showed up
to talk you down

00:11:00.492 --> 00:11:02.094
after you accidentally
ate a whole bag

00:11:02.094 --> 00:11:04.163
of your weird aunt's
pot gummy bears.

00:11:04.163 --> 00:11:05.865
"Stay with me, buddy.
I know you feel like

00:11:05.865 --> 00:11:07.633
your heart's bouncing here
and there and everywhere,

00:11:07.633 --> 00:11:09.134
but this is all going
to be over soon."

00:11:09.134 --> 00:11:11.069
And, even if you take Trump
out of the equation,

00:11:11.069 --> 00:11:13.472
Republicans are all committed
to the project

00:11:13.472 --> 00:11:15.040
and the performance to Trumpism.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:16.542
They're desperate to mimic him.

00:11:16.542 --> 00:11:17.876
That's why GOP politicians,

00:11:17.876 --> 00:11:19.444
like Florida
Governor Ron DeSantis,

00:11:19.444 --> 00:11:21.647
are all trying to imitate
Trump's disastrous handling

00:11:21.647 --> 00:11:24.550
of the coronavirus pandemic,
with DeSantis even going so far

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:26.885
as to ban local governments
and school boards

00:11:26.885 --> 00:11:28.987
from imposing
their own mask mandates.

00:11:28.987 --> 00:11:31.256
-Joe Biden has taken to himself

00:11:31.256 --> 00:11:35.194
to try to single out Florida
over COVID.

00:11:35.194 --> 00:11:36.928
This is a guy who ran
for president

00:11:36.928 --> 00:11:39.998
saying he was going to,
"Shut down the virus."

00:11:39.998 --> 00:11:41.267
And what has he done?

00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:43.835
He's imported more virus
from around the world

00:11:43.835 --> 00:11:46.171
by having a wide open
southern border.

00:11:46.171 --> 00:11:48.407
We can either have
a free society

00:11:48.407 --> 00:11:51.377
or we can have
a biomedical security state.

00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:54.846
And I can tell you,
Florida, we're a free state.

00:11:54.846 --> 00:11:56.882
[ Applause ]
Why don't you get
this border secure

00:11:56.882 --> 00:11:58.450
and, until you do that,

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:02.120
I don't want to hear a blip
about COVID from you.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.255
-Oh, you don't want
to hear a blip

00:12:03.255 --> 00:12:05.390
about a deadly,
highly contagious virus

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:06.892
from the president
of the United States?

00:12:06.892 --> 00:12:08.160
Let me guess --
you'd prefer his thoughts

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.030
on the wokeness
of the U.S. Women's Soccer Team?

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:12.163
Also, when you use
the word blip,

00:12:12.163 --> 00:12:13.732
you sound like an angry grandma

00:12:13.732 --> 00:12:14.933
babysitting her kids.

00:12:14.933 --> 00:12:16.635
"This is knitting time.
I don't want to hear

00:12:16.635 --> 00:12:18.570
another blip
about 'Grand Theft Auto.'

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.806
You can finish Lester's
assassination mission

00:12:20.806 --> 00:12:22.841
after you're done crocheting
this blanket!"

00:12:22.841 --> 00:12:24.676
[ Laughter ]
And I'm no scientist,

00:12:24.676 --> 00:12:26.144
but I do have Google Maps
on my phone

00:12:26.144 --> 00:12:27.946
and I'm pretty sure the border
has nothing to do

00:12:27.946 --> 00:12:29.214
with the Florida COVID surge,

00:12:29.214 --> 00:12:31.683
since the border's like
1,000 miles from Florida.

00:12:31.683 --> 00:12:34.787
You don't get to blame something
that far away for your problems.

00:12:34.787 --> 00:12:37.790
If a kid in Nebraska throws his
Frisbee in the neighbor's lawn,

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:41.260
he can't say it was caught
in the strong winds of La Niña.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.861
Originally written as El Niño,

00:12:42.861 --> 00:12:44.929
but then, we did some research,
found out El Niño?

00:12:44.929 --> 00:12:47.733
Soft winds. And we didn't want
to hear from you guys,

00:12:47.733 --> 00:12:49.969
in "Corrections,"
about how I got it wrong.

00:12:49.969 --> 00:12:51.136
[ Laughter ]

00:12:51.136 --> 00:12:52.438
So we got it right.

00:12:52.438 --> 00:12:56.275
[ Laughter ]

00:12:56.275 --> 00:12:59.044
But, you know, I feel bad
for the people of Florida.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:01.046
They're not as lucky
as we New Yorkers are

00:13:01.046 --> 00:13:03.415
because our governor
is beyond reproach.

00:13:03.415 --> 00:13:04.917
What's that?
[ Laughter ]

00:13:04.917 --> 00:13:06.418
Oh, really?

00:13:06.418 --> 00:13:07.586
A whole report?

00:13:07.586 --> 00:13:10.256
A hundred and sixty-eight pages?

00:13:10.256 --> 00:13:12.091
This is the first
I'm hearing about it.

00:13:12.091 --> 00:13:14.126
Well, I watch CNN.

00:13:14.126 --> 00:13:15.727
Weeknights, 9:00 pm.

00:13:15.727 --> 00:13:17.263
[ Gasp ]
That's his brother?!

00:13:17.263 --> 00:13:20.332
[ Laughter ]

00:13:20.332 --> 00:13:21.633
Back to DeSantis.

00:13:21.633 --> 00:13:24.270
"Biomedical security state"
makes you sound like

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.171
an out-of-work screenwriter
trying to sell

00:13:26.171 --> 00:13:28.340
a sci-fi movie to a director
at a dinner party.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.475
[ As DeSantis ]
It takes place in the year 3049.

00:13:30.475 --> 00:13:32.511
The U.S. is
a biomedical security state

00:13:32.511 --> 00:13:34.880
and the president has to stop
an army of space lizards

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:36.281
who look like Dr. Fauci,

00:13:36.281 --> 00:13:37.916
forcing everyone
to take a vaccine

00:13:37.916 --> 00:13:39.284
that turns them
into Chihuahuas.

00:13:39.284 --> 00:13:41.620
"Why wouldn't the vaccine
also turn them into lizards?"

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.556
Because it ends
with the Taco Bell dog,

00:13:43.556 --> 00:13:44.723
who's the resistance leader,

00:13:44.723 --> 00:13:46.491
looking directly
into the camera and saying,

00:13:46.491 --> 00:13:47.826
"Yo quiero

00:13:47.826 --> 00:13:49.662
freedom."

00:13:49.662 --> 00:13:51.563
[ Laughter ]
"I'm going to go.

00:13:51.563 --> 00:13:52.964
I'm out of ham."

00:13:52.964 --> 00:13:54.967
[ Laughter ]
We

00:13:54.967 --> 00:13:56.268
now have yet another smoking gun

00:13:56.268 --> 00:13:58.204
in the story
of the Trump coup attempt.

00:13:58.204 --> 00:13:59.572
On top of that,
Republican governors

00:13:59.572 --> 00:14:00.872
are actively standing in the way

00:14:00.872 --> 00:14:02.841
of attempts to mitigate
the Delta COVID surge.

00:14:02.841 --> 00:14:03.909
There's a throughline here.

00:14:03.909 --> 00:14:05.810
The party actively
makes things worse

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:07.012
and, when people don't like it,

00:14:07.012 --> 00:14:08.981
they try to subvert democracy
to stay in power,

00:14:08.981 --> 00:14:10.983
even though polls
clearly show that,

00:14:10.983 --> 00:14:13.251
when Trump and the GOP lost,
most Americans...

00:14:13.251 --> 00:14:14.886
-Were happy about it.

00:14:14.886 --> 00:14:16.521
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:16.521 --> 00:14:20.559
♪♪

00:14:20.559 --> 00:14:22.027
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:14:22.027 --> 00:14:23.361
over two million meals a year

00:14:23.361 --> 00:14:25.664
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:14:25.664 --> 00:14:27.165
cancer, and other
serious illnesses

00:14:27.165 --> 00:14:28.667
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:14:28.667 --> 00:14:30.869
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:14:30.869 --> 00:14:33.739
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

